    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "231bb19e_b429cb65",
        "filename": "include/gettimeofday.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1534724
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-13T18:26:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to the [official doc](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/settimeofday.2.html) this should return:\n\n\u003e the number of seconds and microseconds **since the Epoch**\n\nI haven\u0027t looked at [`get_time()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/core/host/timer.c;l\u003d33;drc\u003dd4aa274081c99f3443886977f004721670cc3b35) in details, but is this function a simplified version that returns the number of seconds **since the MCU started**?\n\nIn that case we could add a big disclaimer in the comments to avoid confusion.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "6627decac0c22e744ba063474cc961f0eee2556a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8a93b099_1c17da30",
        "filename": "include/gettimeofday.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
